SUMMARY:Nutcracker: Cast B School Show @ 10:30 AM – ACT I Cast B (Party
  Scene\, Battle Scene\, Snow Scene) (Mandatory – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:Fri. Dec. 11 · Call 9:30 AM · 10:30 AM–11:00 AM · Robins
 on Center\nMANDATORY — production week. CALL TIME 9:30 AM: dancers mus
 t be checked in and backstage by then\, so arrive by 9:15 AM. BA: Call T
 ime is the time dancers should be check-in and backstage - Arrive 15 min
 utes before Call Time.\nACT I Student Matinee Performance (to recorded s
 ound)\; NO COFFEE\, BON BON\, ANGELS.\nAll Casts are called unless a cas
 t is named. SUBJECT TO CHANGE — the BA master schedule\, the weekly BA
  emails and the BA portal are the official source. Master: https://docs.
 google.com/spreadsheets/d/1xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\
 n\nCOSTUME / HAIR / MAKEUP for Lieutenants: Soldiers: Leiutenants — Co
 stume (you provide): Male: Black tights\, black fitted t-shirt Female: B
 lack Seamless Tights\, Black Camisole Leotard\; Shoes: Black Ballet Shoe
 s\; Makeup: Light Stage Makeup\; Hair: Male: Hair out of the eyes Female
 : High Bun\, No Part\; Accessories (BA provides): White Gloves\; Prop (B
 A provides): White gun\nLight Stage Makeup Instruction Sheet:\n•  P
 owder matching skintone\n•  Light brown eye shadow applied to the c
 rease with an eye shadow brush\n•  Dark Brown/Black eyeliner and bl
 ack mascara. No fake lashes.\n•  Blush on the cheeks (be sure to ap
 ply plenty so dancer doesn’t look washed out in the stage lights)\n•
   Red or Dark Red lipstick\nDancers of Color may wear flesh tone tigh
 ts and flesh tone ballet shoes.\nCostume Care Guidelines:\n•  Handl
 e costume pieces with care while changing to prevent damage to delicate 
 fabrics\n•  Promptly notify Ballet Arkansas in the event of costume
  damage at the point of discovery\, no matter how significant\n•  N
 ever throw costumes or accessories on the floor\, or hang costumes by th
 eir elastic straps\n•  Refrain from sitting on the floor while in c
 ostume\n•  Do not attempt to alter\, mend\, clean\, or launder any 
 costume or accessory\n•  Never apply stage make-up while in costume
  and shall take great care to refrain from smudging make-up on costume d
 uring its removal\n•  Refrain from the use of spray perfume or colo
 gne while in costume\n•  Never wear any garment not assigned to cas
 t member\n•  Do not handle or consume food or beverage while in cos
 tume\, with the exception of water\n•  Do not remove costumes from 
 their assigned dressing rooms or from the theater\n•  Remove all bo
 bby pins used to secure head pieces and wigs following their use\n• 
  Return all headpieces to their assigned bags\n•  Comply fully w
 ith any and all updates to Ballet Arkansas’ wardrobe policies\n• 
  Do not pack markers\, paints\, colored drinks or anything that may dama
 ge or stain costumes.
